  "details": "As the title says, this seems to happen when a world is intensive to first load (for example a movie world) and there is also people in it.\nwhat happens in detail is:\n1. you click on a world instance and try to join it\n2. the world will download then try to initialize\n3. after the normal amount of time to initialize vrc will go into its phase of trying to actually load you in\n4. now here vrc will give up and instead shove you into your home world (newest live update seems to throw you in a friends instance of the world you tried to join now)\n5. you are now not in the instance you tried to join\nas a note vrc will not complain about running out of memory or spit any other error messages, and will simply just act like nothing went wrong.\nas a guess this is probably an issue with how god awful the performance of loading in any avatar is (good quality or not) as this isnt something that will happen with an empty instance and will happen even if there is 2 people.\ni hope it isnt an avatar loading performance issue cause if theres anything i dont think ill live long enough to see itll be vrc actually optimizing loading things",
